row(24, 24, 'MATERIAL', f'SHIPS FROM KITTIM — DANIEL QUOTES IT; ASSHUR AND EBER AFFLICTED; THE TRANSLATION NAMES ROME AND THE EUPHRATES. "{H(24, 24, "וצים", "מיד", "כתים")}" ("and SHIPS from the hand of KITTIM" — "ships" (tzim) one seat in this form (Isaiah\'s "gallant ship" its kin); Kittim Javan\'s son (Gen 10:4), the coastland of Isaiah 23 and Ezekiel 27, and DANIEL 11:30 "ships of Kittim shall come against him" — the seer\'s clause quoted in the last prophecy; computed) → {A(24, 24, "וסיען", "יצטרחן", "מרומאי")} ("and LEGIONS shall be gathered FROM THE ROMANS" — Kittim made Rome in the translation\'s text, cut from the shelf\'s bytes); "{H(24, 24, "וענו", "אשור", "וענו", "עבר")}" ("and they afflict Asshur and afflict EBER" — Eber the Hebrews\' eponym, "the father of all the sons of Eber" (Gen 10:21), the same pointing; computed) → {A(24, 24, "ויענון", "לאתור", "וישתעבדון", "לעבר", "פרת")} ("and they afflict Assyria and subjugate BEYOND THE EUPHRATES" — Eber made the river\'s far side, cut); "{H(24, 24, "וגם", "הוא", "עדי", "אבד")}" ("and he too is to destruction" — Amalek\'s clause) → {A(24, 24, "ואף", "אנון", "לעלמא", "ייבדון")} ("and they too shall perish forever"). No narrative verb.')
row(24, 25, 'MATERIAL', f'BALAAM RETURNED TO HIS PLACE; BALAK WENT HIS WAY — JACOB\'S CLAUSE; THE RETELLINGS. "{H(24, 25, "ויקם", "בלעם", "וילך", "וישב", "למקמו")}" ("and Balaam rose and went and returned to his place" — the clause with the Philistines\' ark and David\'s Barzillai; he is found among Midian at 31:8, killed by the sword; computed) → {A(24, 25, "וקם", "בלעם", "ואזל", "ותב", "לאתריה")} ("and Balaam rose and went and returned to his place"); "{H(24, 25, "וגם", "בלק", "הלך", "לדרכו")}" ("and Balak too went his way" — JACOB\'s clause, "and Jacob went his way, and angels of God met him" (Gen 32:2), the phrase\'s two Torah seats; THE RETELLINGS: "the LORD turned the curse into a blessing" (Deut 23:6, Neh 13:2), "I would not listen to Balaam" (Josh 24:10), Jephthah\'s "are you better than Balak son of Zippor?" (Judg 11:25), Micah\'s "what Balak counseled and what Balaam answered — from SHITTIM to Gilgal" (6:5); computed) → {A(24, 25, "ואף", "בלק", "אזל", "לארחיה")} ("and Balak too went his way"). The register: "and he rose", "and he went", "and he returned".')
